  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nPeriods of showers and storms today, although hopefully not as \nnumerous in coverage as Friday. A series of shortwaves moving \nthrough the area, one expected this morning/early afternoon, \nfollowed by another later on in the evening, will once again \ngenerate showers and storms across the area. An isolated storm could \nbecome severe, with a wind threat, and naturally, in the very moist \nenvironment, heavy downpours will continue to be a threat. \n\nThere may be a brief lull in convective activity on Sunday as some \nmodels are indicating weak high pressure taking hold, although \nchances will still remain, mainly across the far south from a \npassing wave. However, activity looks to ramp back up again Monday \nthrough the remainder of the extended, as broad troughing takes hold \nacross the eastern U.S., with multiple waves of convection moving \ninto the area on west-northwesterly flow. Some of these complexes \nwill have the potential for strong damaging winds as deep layer \nshear increases, as we progress into mid week in particular, and of \ncourse, localized flooding issues, particularly in spots that \nreceive repetitive rounds of convection.",
